nodes.body:
Fixed the two native CI failures in the latest commit. The shared host now uses a serializable `None` default for `table_strides`; runtime binders continue supplying the tuple. The missing-page-argument test now removes the required ABI slot explicitly instead of assuming the shared host lacks paged support.

Added a separate prefill artifact-reload detector: the existing short-Q D256 fixture selects decode, so it could not detect this prefill-host persistence regression. The new test asserts the actual prefill module and forbids compilation in the second process. Parent fails; candidate passes. The focused run has 13 passing checks, including both corrected CI checks, fresh-process artifact reload, and two paged lifecycle cases; zero failures or skips. All kernel function bodies are unchanged. Changed-file hooks pass.

@cudnn-ci-bot run python/sdpa/frost

